---
export const title = 'Many slides';
export const order = 300;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';

const steps = Array.from({ length: 9 }, (_, i) => i + 1);
---

<p>
  With up to seven pages, each page has a picker button. With more, a "3 of 9" counter takes their
  place, so the row of controls stays short.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; max-width: 480px;'>
    <wc-carousel label='Getting started'>
      {steps.map(step => (
        <div aria-label={`Step ${step} of 9`} style='display: grid; place-items: center; height: 160px; border-radius: 16px; background: var(--color-secondary-container); color: var(--color-on-secondary-container);' class='text-headline-small'>
          Step {step}
        </div>
      ))}
    </wc-carousel>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Accessibility</h3>
<p>
  The carousel is a region named by <code>label</code> and announced as a carousel. Each slide is a
  group announced as a slide and named "2 of 5", unless it has an <code>aria-label</code> of its own,
  as these do. The pickers are buttons named "Slide 3 of 9", or "Slides 4 to 6 of 9" with
  <code>per-view</code>, and the current one has <code>aria-current</code>. Previous and next stay
  focusable at the ends, with <code>aria-disabled</code>, so focus never drops to the page.
</p>
